WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.280
It's May 25th, 2026, and I'm Patrick in Vancouver.

00:00:04.840 --> 00:00:07.220
A new week and plenty happening with Tesla.

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:11.920
Tesla's rebrand of FSD to assisted driving in China

00:00:11.920 --> 00:00:16.340
shows how local regulators are forcing clearer limits on autonomy claims.

00:00:17.260 --> 00:00:20.200
Tesla changed the name of its full self-driving software

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:23.240
to Tesla assisted driving for the China market.

00:00:23.880 --> 00:00:27.120
The move aligns the product label with stricter local rules

00:00:27.120 --> 00:00:30.940
that treat higher levels of automation as advanced driver assistance

00:00:30.940 --> 00:00:33.280
rather than autonomous operation.

00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.000
It affects how the feature is marketed

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:38.740
and what drivers are told to expect during use.

00:00:39.640 --> 00:00:42.040
The change comes as Tesla continues to expand

00:00:42.040 --> 00:00:44.920
supervised FSD capabilities in the country.

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.720
Regulators in other markets may watch

00:00:47.720 --> 00:00:49.760
whether similar naming adjustments follow.

00:00:50.600 --> 00:00:52.600
Taking a step back from today's headlines,

00:00:52.920 --> 00:00:56.460
the shift in how Tesla labels its driver assistance software in China,

00:00:56.460 --> 00:01:00.340
challenges the assumption that a single global autonomy narrative

00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:02.460
can travel unchanged across markets.

00:01:03.120 --> 00:01:05.240
Regulators there now require wording

00:01:05.240 --> 00:01:07.380
that keeps the driver firmly in the loop,

00:01:07.960 --> 00:01:09.980
even as the underlying code improves.

00:01:10.960 --> 00:01:13.460
The data point that matters is the explicit separation

00:01:14.020 --> 00:01:16.860
between marketing language and technical capability,

00:01:17.520 --> 00:01:19.980
where earlier versions used full self-driving

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:22.660
the new label stresses assistance only.

00:01:22.660 --> 00:01:26.140
This forces the same neural net stack to operate

00:01:26.140 --> 00:01:29.500
under tighter consumer expectations and legal exposure

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:33.560
without any change to the actual miles of training data behind it.

00:01:34.280 --> 00:01:37.020
Tesla's vertical integration gives it a direct path

00:01:37.020 --> 00:01:41.840
to adjust both the user interface and the regulatory filing in one cycle.

00:01:42.620 --> 00:01:44.880
That structure lets the company test whether

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:47.260
clearer labeling reduces intervention rates

00:01:47.260 --> 00:01:50.160
or simply changes how drivers allocate attention.

00:01:50.160 --> 00:01:53.380
Something competitors without end-to-end control

00:01:53.380 --> 00:01:56.580
over software and vehicle hardware cannot match as quickly.

00:01:57.500 --> 00:02:00.600
The driver who completed a record US coast-to-coast

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:04.620
FSD supervised trip has started a similar run across Canada.

00:02:05.260 --> 00:02:08.540
The journey tests how the system handles varying road conditions,

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:11.020
signage and weather between provinces.

00:02:11.680 --> 00:02:13.540
It also checks performance on routes

00:02:13.540 --> 00:02:16.600
with fewer mapped updates than major US corridors.

00:02:17.600 --> 00:02:19.600
Success would extend the documented range

00:02:19.600 --> 00:02:21.680
of supervised long distance travel.

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:24.360
The next data point will be completion time

00:02:24.360 --> 00:02:26.080
and any interventions required.

00:02:26.900 --> 00:02:29.480
Owners have shared UI mockups to address cases

00:02:29.480 --> 00:02:32.380
where FSD supervised struggles to select

00:02:32.380 --> 00:02:34.600
or execute a final parking spot.

00:02:35.500 --> 00:02:38.620
Tesla is expected to favor a simpler preference setting

00:02:38.620 --> 00:02:41.100
approach over complex on-screen choices.

00:02:41.720 --> 00:02:45.780
The issue arises most often in lots with multiple open spaces

00:02:45.780 --> 00:02:47.240
or unclear markings.

00:02:47.840 --> 00:02:51.120
A fix would reduce the number of times drivers must take over

00:02:51.120 --> 00:02:52.000
at the end of a trip.

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:56.280
The next software update will show whether the company adopts

00:02:56.280 --> 00:02:57.740
any of the community suggestions.

00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:02.380
Recent FSD supervised clips show the car reducing speed

00:03:02.380 --> 00:03:05.240
and merging into regular traffic when a police vehicle

00:03:05.240 --> 00:03:06.580
is visible in the median.

00:03:07.540 --> 00:03:11.100
The behavior matches common driver habits around law enforcement.

00:03:11.540 --> 00:03:15.060
It emerged from training data rather than an explicit rule change.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:18.300
The update demonstrates how the system continues

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.360
to absorb subtle road etiquette.

00:03:20.700 --> 00:03:23.900
Further clips will reveal whether the response stays consistent

00:03:23.900 --> 00:03:24.820
across regions.

00:03:25.720 --> 00:03:29.480
Aftermarket kits allow cyber truck buyers to add off-road equipment

00:03:29.480 --> 00:03:32.400
that brings the total added cost to $18,000.

00:03:33.000 --> 00:03:36.920
The packages include upgraded suspension, auxiliary lighting

00:03:36.920 --> 00:03:40.540
and storage solutions designed for extended remote travel.

00:03:41.100 --> 00:03:43.480
They target owners who want more capability

00:03:43.480 --> 00:03:46.060
than the standard truck provides out of the box.

00:03:46.900 --> 00:03:49.780
Demand for these conversions will test how many buyers

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:52.120
treat the vehicle as a base for customization.

00:03:53.120 --> 00:03:56.480
Sales figures from the suppliers will give an early read on uptake.

00:03:57.420 --> 00:04:00.680
A stripped Tesla chassis was turned into a functional go-kart

00:04:00.680 --> 00:04:02.600
using the original battery and motors.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:05.440
The build keeps the electric powertrain

00:04:05.440 --> 00:04:08.240
while removing all bodywork and interior components.

00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:11.960
It demonstrates how accessible the core hardware remains

00:04:11.960 --> 00:04:14.880
for custom projects even after major disassembly.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:18.080
The finished cart was tested on a small track

00:04:18.080 --> 00:04:19.620
to verify a drivability.

00:04:20.240 --> 00:04:23.220
Similar projects may increase if more wrecked or donor

00:04:23.220 --> 00:04:24.640
Tesla's become available.

00:04:25.400 --> 00:04:28.140
A simple hardware adjustment was posted that removes

00:04:28.140 --> 00:04:31.260
common calibration steps during starlink installation.

00:04:31.920 --> 00:04:34.960
The breakdown shows how the change could speed up field deployments

00:04:35.480 --> 00:04:36.460
for new terminals.

00:04:37.220 --> 00:04:40.080
Owners following the steps reported faster setup times

00:04:40.080 --> 00:04:41.280
without extra tools.

00:04:42.060 --> 00:04:45.580
Tesla shared a direct link to schedule a no obligation drive.

00:04:46.120 --> 00:04:48.940
The post keeps the focus on letting potential buyers

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:51.000
experience the car's first hand.

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:55.560
It arrives as more competitors launch new models in the same segments.

00:04:56.660 --> 00:04:59.860
Test meals of lucids upcoming lower priced SUV

00:04:59.860 --> 00:05:02.120
were photographed beside a Model Y.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.200
The sighting confirms development continues

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:07.720
on a vehicle aimed at a wider buyer group.

00:05:07.720 --> 00:05:10.860
Size comparison suggests it will compete directly

00:05:10.860 --> 00:05:12.880
in the popular crossover segment.

00:05:13.440 --> 00:05:17.200
The name change reflects tighter Chinese rules on what can be marketed

00:05:17.200 --> 00:05:18.500
as autonomous driving.

00:05:19.080 --> 00:05:22.180
It limits how Tesla can describe the system's capabilities

00:05:22.180 --> 00:05:23.160
to local buyers.

00:05:23.780 --> 00:05:27.380
The company will need to maintain the same supervised safety case

00:05:27.380 --> 00:05:29.760
while meeting clearer labeling requirements.

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:33.860
Future software releases will show whether the adjusted branding

00:05:33.860 --> 00:05:36.340
affects uptake or driver expectations.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:40.660
Before we go, keep an eye on completion time and interventions

